{
  "case_id": "2006-06-313",
  "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "While this Court has laid out a framework for reviewing prosecutors' closing arguments, the fairness standard established in Donnelly and Darden is by its nature a very general standard. Under this Court's interpretation of AEDPA, the State court should therefore be provided more leeway in reaching outcomes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask one sort of preliminary question. Supposing the prosecutor misstated the law in his closing argument. Would that be reviewable in this Court under AEDPA?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think his argument here contained any misstatements of the law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, none of the comments misstated the evidence nor did they misstate the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the relevance of that argument otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why is it improper for, for the prosecution to argue that, given the facts of this case, given the aggravating factors and the lack of mitigating factors, the brutality of the crime, the only sensible decision for you ladies and gentlemen of the jury is the death penalty? That's an improper argument? Doesn't that amount to saying you have a duty to come back with the death penalty? Why can't the prosecution argue that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's certainly not improper to make statements based on inferences from the evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, do you think the Patton argument has anything to do with the evidence? I mean, the Patton argument -- correct me if I'm wrong, but I thought the argument that referred to General Patton was an argument that, number one, talked about his addressing the troops before battle. And he was telling the troops that unfortunately it is sometimes their duty to kill. And he said: Go out there and do your duty, which I assume any reasonable listener would say, go out there and kill."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And finally, the last instruction that the jury heard before closing arguments was that closing arguments were not evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 0.6,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "It is counterintuitive to assume that the jury disregarded those instructions as a whole and instead improperly relied on the prosecutor's closing argument when they declined to find the one aggravating circumstance that the prosecutor spoke most about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I go back to my question? Because there's a legal question here about what law we can look to under AEDPA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. Spillars",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was a habeas petition filed prior to AEDPA, but it was dismissed and he did not appeal from that. This was filed after AEDPA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "the respondent has not asserted that argument, that AEDPA does not apply in this case. And for good reason, because --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As the former prosecutor's brief makes clear, George \"Buzz\" Westfall's penalty phase closing argument in Mr. Weaver's case contained a number of improper and mutually reinforcing statements which exploited the authority of his office, analogized the jury's duties to that of soldiers in war time, injected extraneous matters into the proceedings, and appealed to the jurors' passions and prejudice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think they overstated the significance of Viereck. Isn't Viereck -- does Viereck stand, do you think, for a per se rule that a prosecutor in a closing argument may never mention the word soldier?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "the Missouri Supreme Court in this case said the decision was unreasonable because it failed to consider significant portions of Mr. Weaver's challenge to this argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the death penalty in this case solely for deterrent reasons, i.e., reasons unanchored in the culpability of this particular defendant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. BLUME",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0001-0011",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He appealed the improper dismissal of his petition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Even -- even the Supreme Court cases going to the other points, they didn't -- did any of them involve a separate penalty phase?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Blume",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't see any reason why a principle which this Court has repeatedly reaffirmed that a prosecutor is not supposed to leverage his opinion and the prestige of his office behind a particular outcome, would apply any less at the penalty phase of a capital trial than at the guilt phase of a capital trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90c63a856e4b811da1297f61d13df3eb94cc56fcd3f8123c9b5301186dd47faa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90c63a856e4b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-06-313",
      "confidence": 0.0,
